# Programmatically generated De Almeida Qs

section1_en = [{'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'Who was appointed as the first Portuguese Viceroy of India by King Manuel I in 1505?', 'opts': ['Francisco de Almeida', 'Afonso de Albuquerque', 'Vasco da Gama', 'Pedro Álvares Cabral'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Francisco de Almeida was commissioned as the first Viceroy in 1505 to establish permanent governance.'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'In which month of 1505 did Francisco de Almeida depart from Lisbon with a fleet of 21 ships?', 'opts': ['March 1505', 'May 1505', 'September 1505', 'December 1505'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Almeida departed Lisbon on March 25, 1505, with a massive fleet to consolidate trade.'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': "What was the term duration of Francisco de Almeida's initial appointment as Viceroy?", 'opts': ['Three years', 'Five years', 'One year', 'Ten years'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'He was appointed for a standard three-year term by the Portuguese crown.'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'Which Portuguese king signed the royal directives appointing Almeida as the Viceroy of the Estado da Índia?', 'opts': ['King Manuel I', 'King John II', 'King Sebastian', 'King Philip I'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'King Manuel I signed the commission establishing the permanent viceroyalty.'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'What specific political title was bestowed upon Francisco de Almeida upon his departure from Portugal?', 'opts': ['Viceroy of India', 'Governor-General of Malacca', 'Admiral of the Red Sea', 'Captain-Major of Calicut'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': "He was given the title of Viceroy of India, representing the King's sovereign authority."}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'Which goals were set in the royal instructions given to Viceroy Almeida in 1505? (Select all that apply)', 'opts': ['Build fortresses along East Africa and Western India', 'Destroy Mamluk trade monopoly in the Indian Ocean', 'Capture Malacca immediately in the first year', 'Sign peace treaties with Calicut immediately'], 'ans': [0, 1], 'sol': 'The instructions focused on fortresses (Kilwa, Anjadip, Cannanore, Cochin) and breaking Muslim naval dominance. Malacca was not a priority in the first year.'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': "Identify the elements of Almeida's commission as first Viceroy. (Select all that apply)", 'opts': ['Standard three-year term', 'Direct representation of King Manuel I', 'Command of a 21-ship armada', 'Total control over inland conquests of Northern India'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'Almeida had a three-year term, represented the King, and led 21 ships. Inland conquest of Northern India was not authorized.'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': "Which classes of officers sailed under Almeida's command in 1505? (Select all that apply)", 'opts': ['Military knights and noblemen', 'Franciscan friars', 'Skilled pilots and cartographers', 'Spanish conquistadors'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'His fleet carried nobles, soldiers, friars, and experienced pilots. Spanish conquistadors did not sail with them.'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'What strategic dilemmas did Almeida face regarding the viceroyalty system? (Select all that apply)', 'opts': ['Logistical delays in communicating with Lisbon', 'Rivalry and command disputes with Afonso de Albuquerque', 'Lack of sufficient soldiers to garrison multiple forts', 'Rebellion from the Portuguese home parliament'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'Communication delays, disputes with Albuquerque, and garrison shortages were primary operational challenges.'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'Select the geographical focus areas mentioned in the 1505 royal instructions to Almeida. (Select all that apply)', 'opts': ['The Malabar Coast of India', 'The East African Swahili Coast', 'The island of Anjadip', 'The mainland of China'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'Malabar, Swahili Coast, and Anjadip were crucial targets. China was not targeted by Almeida.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Francisco de Almeida was the second Viceroy but the first Governor of India.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'He was the first Viceroy and Governor; no one held the title before him.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'King Manuel I selected Francisco de Almeida because of his military experience in the Granada wars.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'Almeida was a distinguished soldier who fought against the Moors in Granada.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Almeida refused to accept any title other than Captain-Major during his voyage.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'He accepted the official title of Viceroy, which granted him full royal representation.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The viceroyalty was established to replace the system of temporary annual trading fleets.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'It provided a permanent administrative and military presence in the Indian Ocean.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Almeida was instructed to establish a permanent capital at Goa in 1505.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'Goa was not yet captured; the instructions directed building forts at Cochin, Cannanore, and Anjadip.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The viceroyalty commission of 1505 did not grant Almeida the power to sign treaties with local rulers.', 'ans': False, 'sol': "He had full plenipotentiary powers to sign treaties in the King's name."}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Francisco de Almeida was succeeded directly by Afonso de Albuquerque.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'Albuquerque succeeded him, although Almeida delayed the transfer of power.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Almeida belonged to one of the most prominent noble families in Portugal.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'He was a member of the elite Count of Abrantes family.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'Francisco de Almeida belonged to the noble family of the Counts of __________.', 'ans': 'Abrantes', 'sol': 'He was a high-born noble from the Counts of Abrantes family.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The Portuguese monarch who appointed Francisco de Almeida in 1505 was King __________.', 'ans': 'Manuel I', 'sol': 'King Manuel I established the permanent viceroyalty.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'Almeida set sail from the port of Lisbon in March __________.', 'ans': '1505', 'sol': 'He departed on March 25, 1505 CE.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The first base established by Almeida in East Africa in 1505 was at __________.', 'ans': 'Kilwa', 'sol': 'He fortified Kilwa to secure the Swahili Coast passage.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'Almeida was granted the supreme title of __________ to represent the Crown in Asia.', 'ans': 'Viceroy', 'sol': 'Viceroy was the highest administrative title given.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': "The viceroyl's commission was initially limited to a duration of __________ years.", 'ans': 'three', 'sol': 'A three-year term was standard to prevent consolidation of independent power.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The military adversary that Almeida was specifically instructed to neutralize at sea was the __________ Empire.', 'ans': 'Mamluk', 'sol': 'The Mamluk Sultanate of Egypt controlled the spice monopoly.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The successor who arrived to replace Almeida in 1508 was Afonso de __________.', 'ans': 'Albuquerque', 'sol': 'Albuquerque arrived with royal orders to take over as governor.'}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': 'Match the 1505 expedition details with their quantities:', 'items': [{'left': 'Number of ships'}, {'left': 'Number of soldiers/men'}, {'left': 'Term of appointment'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': '21 vessels'}, {'val': '1', 'text': '1,500 troops'}, {'val': '2', 'text': '3 years'}], 'sol': 'Almeida departed with 21 ships, 1,500 men, for a 3-year term.'}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': 'Match the historical personalities with their administrative roles:', 'items': [{'left': 'King Manuel I'}, {'left': 'Francisco de Almeida'}, {'left': 'Afonso de Albuquerque'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': 'Sponsoring monarch'}, {'val': '1', 'text': 'First appointed Viceroy'}, {'val': '2', 'text': 'Designated second Governor'}], 'sol': 'King Manuel I was the sponsor, Almeida the first Viceroy, and Albuquerque the second Governor.'}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': "Match the geographical milestones of Almeida's 1505 voyage with their order:", 'items': [{'left': 'Departure port'}, {'left': 'East African stop'}, {'left': 'Indian Ocean island base'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': 'Lisbon harbor'}, {'val': '1', 'text': 'Kilwa fortress'}, {'val': '2', 'text': 'Anjadip Island'}], 'sol': 'He departed Lisbon, fortified Kilwa, and anchored at Anjadip.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': "What is the exact date of departure for Almeida's viceregal fleet from Lisbon?", 'sol': 'Answer: March 25, 1505. Explanation: The fleet left Restelo on March 25, 1505 CE.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': "Who was the Portuguese Viceroy's son who accompanied him on the 1505 voyage?", 'sol': 'Answer: Lourenço de Almeida. Explanation: Lourenço served as a principal captain under his father.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Which battle in Europe gave Almeida the military reputation required for the viceroyalty?', 'sol': 'Answer: The Battle of Toro. Explanation: Almeida showed outstanding valor in the Battle of Toro (1476).'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'What was the name of the state entity established by the Portuguese Crown to govern Asian trade?', 'sol': 'Answer: Estado da Índia. Explanation: The Estado da Índia was the formal state entity.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': "Why did the King restrict the viceroy's term to just three years?", 'sol': 'Answer: To prevent the viceroy from establishing independent power. Explanation: Short tenures ensured absolute loyalty to Lisbon.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Where did Almeida make his first land claim in India?', 'sol': 'Answer: Anjadip Island. Explanation: He landed and began fortification at Anjadip island first.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Which family of Portuguese nobility did Almeida marry into?', 'sol': 'Answer: The family of Lanções. Explanation: He married Maria de Noronha, connected to high nobility.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': "What was the primary merchant council in Lisbon that regulated the Viceroy's trade cargos?", 'sol': 'Answer: Casa da Índia. Explanation: Casa da Índia managed all imperial cargoes and imports.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: King Manuel I appointed Francisco de Almeida as the first Viceroy in 1505.\nReason: The Portuguese Crown wanted to replace temporary fleets with a permanent administration in India.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'The viceroyalty was created to manage trade permanently.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: Almeida was given a standard three-year term of office.\nReason: King Manuel I feared that longer tenures would encourage viceroys to declare independence.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Term limits were standard administrative tools for imperial control.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': "Assertion: Lourenço de Almeida served as a key naval commander under the Viceroy.\nReason: He was Francisco de Almeida's only son and a trusted military lieutenant.", 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Lourenço led many crucial patrols on behalf of his father.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: The viceregal instructions ordered the immediate capture of Goa.\nReason: Goa was the primary administrative base of the Mamluk Sultanate in 1505.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 3, 'sol': 'Both statements are false. Goa was not mentioned in the 1505 instructions, and it was under Bijapur, not Mamluks.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': "Assertion: Francisco de Almeida delayed hand over of power to Afonso de Albuquerque in 1508.\nReason: Almeida disputed the validity of Albuquerque's credentials and sought revenge for his son's death.", 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Almeida refused to step down until he destroyed the Mamluk fleet at Diu.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: The fleet of 1505 carried a large number of Franciscan friars.\nReason: The Portuguese expansion combined commercial monopoly goals with Christian missionary zeal.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Religious conversions and missionary presence were integral to Portuguese state policy.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: The Estado da Índia was established as a private joint-stock corporation.\nReason: The King wanted to minimize financial risks to the royal treasury.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 3, 'sol': 'Both are false. The Estado da Índia was a state-owned crown monopoly, not a private corporation.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'Assertion: Almeida participated in the conquest of Granada before his appointment.\nReason: Military experience against Muslim states in Spain and North Africa was highly valued by the Portuguese Crown.', 'opts': ['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A', 'Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A', 'A is true but R is false', 'A is false but R is true'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': "Almeida's experience in the Reconquista made him the ideal candidate to fight Mamluks."}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'Consider the following statements regarding the appointment of Francisco de Almeida:\n1. He was the first Viceroy of the Estado da Índia.\n2. His appointment was sponsored by King John II in 1498.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. Statement 2 is incorrect; he was appointed by King Manuel I in 1505.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'Consider the following statements about the 1505 expedition:\n1. The fleet consisted of 21 ships carrying 1,500 soldiers.\n2. The expedition departed from the port of Porto.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. Statement 2 is incorrect; they departed from Lisbon.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'With reference to the viceregal term of office, consider these statements:\n1. It was set to a non-renewable period of ten years.\n2. Scribes and factors were directly answerable to the Viceroy rather than Lisbon.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2'], 'ans': 3, 'sol': 'Both statements are incorrect. The term was three years, and factors were directly responsible to the Crown (Casa da Índia).'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': "Consider the statements about Francisco de Almeida's early life:\n1. He gained fame at the Battle of Toro in 1476.\n2. He fought against the Moors in Granada under the Spanish Monarchs.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?", 'opts': ['1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2'], 'ans': 2, 'sol': 'Both statements are correct. Almeida was a veteran of both the Portuguese-Castilian wars and the Granada Reconquista.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'With reference to the successor of the first Viceroy, consider these statements:\n1. Afonso de Albuquerque was designated as the second Governor.\n2. Almeida welcomed Albuquerque immediately and transferred all powers in Cochin.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['1 only', '2 only', 'Both 1 and 2', 'Neither 1 nor 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. Statement 2 is incorrect; Almeida refused to hand over power and imprisoned Albuquerque.'}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why did King Manuel I establish a permanent viceroyalty in India in 1505?', 'sol': 'To secure the trade routes, manage permanent factories, and counter the Mamluk naval monopoly with a unified military command.'}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why did Almeida refuse to immediately hand over power to Afonso de Albuquerque in 1508?', 'sol': "Almeida wanted to avenge the death of his son Lourenço at Chaul and questioned the validity of Albuquerque's secret patents."}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why was a three-year term limit imposed on the office of the Portuguese Viceroy?', 'sol': 'To prevent the viceroy from developing a local power base or declaring independence from the Lisbon Crown.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': 'How did the creation of the Estado da Índia change Portuguese operations in the Indian Ocean?', 'sol': 'It transitioned their operations from temporary, seasonal trading expeditions to a permanent political and military administration.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': "How did Almeida's family connections in Portugal influence his appointment as Viceroy?", 'sol': 'As a member of the Counts of Abrantes family, he had direct access to King Manuel I, making him a trusted noble commander.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': 'How did Almeida assert royal authority over Portuguese merchants operating in India?', 'sol': 'He enforced strict cargo logs, centralized spice purchases at the royal factories, and cracked down on private trade.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': 'Examine the logistical challenges of maintaining a viceroyalty in Cochin from Lisbon.', 'sol': 'Communication took months, reinforcements were seasonal, and the Viceroy had to act autonomously during crises.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': 'Analyze the conflict between Almeida and Albuquerque regarding the transition of power in 1508-1509.', 'sol': 'The conflict illustrated the clash between two different strategies of empire-building and the problem of verifying royal patents overseas.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': 'Evaluate the strategic selection of Francisco de Almeida based on his Reconquista military background.', 'sol': 'His experience in Granada made him highly effective at combatting Muslim coalitions but less inclined towards territorial expansion in India.'}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': 'Explain the structure and authority of the Estado da Índia established in 1505.', 'sol': "It was a state-run imperial organization in Asia, headed by a Viceroy who held civil, judicial, and military powers in the King's name."}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': "Describe the role of the 'Capitão-Mor' (Captain-Major) under the Viceroyalty.", 'sol': "The Capitão-Mor commanded individual fleets and patrols, enforcing the Viceroy's naval policies and protecting trade bases."}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': 'Explain why the Portuguese Crown prioritized naval governance over land acquisitions in 1505.', 'sol': "Maintaining sea supremacy was cheaper, utilized Portugal's naval technology, and avoided costly conflicts with large Indian mainland states."}]

section1_hi = [{'type': 'MCQ', 'q': '1505 में राजा मैनुअल प्रथम द्वारा भारत के पहले पुर्तगाली वायसराय के रूप में किसे नियुक्त किया गया था?', 'opts': ['फ्रांसिस्को डी अल्मेडा', 'अल्फांसो डी अल्बुकर्क', 'वास्को डी गामा', 'पेड्रो अल्वारेज़ कैब्राल'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'फ्रांसिस्को डी अल्मेडा को स्थायी शासन स्थापित करने के लिए 1505 में पहले वायसराय के रूप में नियुक्त किया गया था।'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'फ्रांसिस्को डी अल्मेडा 21 जहाजों के बेड़े के साथ मार्च 1505 में लिस्बन से किस महीने रवाना हुए थे?', 'opts': ['मार्च 1505', 'मई 1505', 'सितंबर 1505', 'दिसंबर 1505'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'अल्मेडा व्यापार को मजबूत करने के लिए 25 मार्च, 1505 को एक विशाल बेड़े के साथ लिस्बन से रवाना हुए थे।'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'वायसराय के रूप में फ्रांसिस्को डी अल्मेडा की प्रारंभिक नियुक्ति की अवधि क्या थी?', 'opts': ['तीन वर्ष', 'पांच वर्ष', 'एक वर्ष', 'दस वर्ष'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'उन्हें पुर्तगाली क्राउन द्वारा मानक तीन साल के कार्यकाल के लिए नियुक्त किया गया था।'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'किस पुर्तगाली राजा ने अल्मेडा को एस्टाडो दा इंडिया के वायसराय के रूप में नियुक्त करने वाले शाही निर्देशों पर हस्ताक्षर किए?', 'opts': ['राजा मैनुअल प्रथम', 'राजा जॉन द्वितीय', 'राजा सेबेस्टियन', 'राजा फिलिप प्रथम'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'राजा मैनुअल प्रथम ने स्थायी वायसराय पद की स्थापना करने वाले आयोग पर हस्ताक्षर किए थे।'}, {'type': 'MCQ', 'q': 'पुर्तगाल से प्रस्थान के समय फ्रांसिस्को डी अल्मेडा को कौन सी विशिष्ट राजनीतिक उपाधि प्रदान की गई थी?', 'opts': ['भारत के वायसराय', 'मलक्का के गवर्नर-जनरल', 'लाल सागर के एडमिरल', 'कालीकट के कैप्टन-मेजर'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'उन्हें भारत के वायसराय की उपाधि दी गई थी, जो राजा के संप्रभु अधिकार का प्रतिनिधित्व करती थी।'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': '1505 में वायसराय अल्मेडा को दिए गए शाही निर्देशों में कौन से लक्ष्य निर्धारित किए गए थे? (सभी लागू विकल्प चुनें)', 'opts': ['पूर्वी अफ्रीका और पश्चिमी भारत के साथ किले बनाना', 'हिंद महासागर में ममलुक व्यापार एकाधिकार को नष्ट करना', 'पहले ही वर्ष में मलक्का पर तुरंत कब्जा करना', 'कालीकट के साथ तुरंत शांति संधियों पर हस्ताक्षर करना'], 'ans': [0, 1], 'sol': 'निर्देशों में किलों (किलवा, अंजादीप, कन्नूर, कोचीन) के निर्माण और मुस्लिम नौसैनिक वर्चस्व को तोड़ने पर ध्यान केंद्रित किया गया था।'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'पहले वायसराय के रूप में अल्मेडा के आयोग के तत्वों की पहचान करें। (सभी लागू विकल्प चुनें)', 'opts': ['मानक तीन साल का कार्यकाल', 'राजा मैनुअल प्रथम का सीधा प्रतिनिधित्व', '21 जहाजों के बेड़े की कमान', 'उत्तरी भारत के अंतर्देशीय विजय पर पूर्ण नियंत्रण'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'अल्मेडा का कार्यकाल तीन वर्ष का था, उन्होंने राजा का प्रतिनिधित्व किया और 21 जहाजों का नेतृत्व किया। अंतर्देशीय विजय उनके एजेंडे में नहीं थी।'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': '1505 में अल्मेडा की कमान में किस वर्ग के अधिकारी रवाना हुए थे? (सभी लागू विकल्प चुनें)', 'opts': ['सैन्य शूरवीर और रईस', 'फ्रांसिस्कन तपस्वी', 'कुशल पायलट और मानचित्रकार', 'स्पेनिश विजेता'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'उनके बेड़े में रईस, सैनिक, तपस्वी और अनुभवी पायलट शामिल थे। स्पेनिश विजेता उनके साथ नहीं थे।'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'वायसराय प्रणाली के संबंध में अल्मेडा को किन रणनीतिक दुविधाओं का सामना करना पड़ा? (सभी लागू विकल्प चुनें)', 'opts': ['लिस्बन के साथ संचार में रसद देरी', 'अल्फांसो डी अल्बुकर्क के साथ प्रतिद्वंद्विता और कमान विवाद', 'कई किलों की रक्षा के लिए पर्याप्त सैनिकों की कमी', 'पुर्तगाली संसद से विद्रोह'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'संचार में देरी, अल्बुकर्क के साथ विवाद और सैनिकों की कमी प्राथमिक परिचालन चुनौतियाँ थीं।'}, {'type': 'Multiple Correct MCQ', 'q': 'अल्मेडा को दिए गए 1505 के शाही निर्देशों में उल्लिखित भौगोलिक फोकस क्षेत्रों का चयन करें। (सभी लागू विकल्प चुनें)', 'opts': ['भारत का मालाबार तट', 'पूर्वी अफ्रीकी स्वाहिली तट', 'अंजादीप द्वीप', 'चीन की मुख्य भूमि'], 'ans': [0, 1, 2], 'sol': 'मालाबार, स्वाहिली तट और अंजादीप प्रमुख लक्ष्य थे। चीन अल्मेडा के निशाने पर नहीं था।'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'फ्रांसिस्को डी अल्मेडा was the second वायसराय but the first Governor of भारत.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'He was the first वायसराय and Governor; no one held the title before him.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'राजा मैनुअल प्रथम selected फ्रांसिस्को डी अल्मेडा because of his military experience in the Granada wars.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'अल्मेडा was a distinguished soldier who fought against the Moors in Granada.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Almeida refused to accept any title other than Captain-Major during his voyage.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'He accepted the official title of वायसराय, which granted him full royal representation.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The viceroyalty was established to replace the system of temporary annual trading fleets.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'It provided a permanent administrative and military presence in the Indian Ocean.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Almeida was instructed to establish a permanent capital at Goa in 1505.', 'ans': False, 'sol': 'Goa was not yet captured; the instructions directed building forts at Cochin, Cannanore, and Anjadip.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'The viceroyalty commission of 1505 did not grant Almeida the power to sign treaties with local rulers.', 'ans': False, 'sol': "He had full plenipotentiary powers to sign treaties in the King's name."}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'फ्रांसिस्को डी अल्मेडा was succeeded directly by Afonso de Albuquerque.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'Albuquerque succeeded him, although अल्मेडा delayed the transfer of power.'}, {'type': 'True/False', 'q': 'Almeida belonged to one of the most prominent noble families in पुर्तगाल.', 'ans': True, 'sol': 'He was a member of the elite Count of Abrantes family.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'फ्रांसिस्को डी अल्मेडा belonged to the noble family of the Counts of __________.', 'ans': 'Abrantes', 'sol': 'He was a high-born noble from the Counts of Abrantes family.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The Portuguese monarch who appointed फ्रांसिस्को डी अल्मेडा in 1505 was King __________.', 'ans': 'Manuel I', 'sol': 'King Manuel I established the permanent viceroyalty.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'Almeida set sail from the port of Lisbon in March __________.', 'ans': '1505', 'sol': 'He departed on March 25, 1505 CE.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The first base established by Almeida in East Africa in 1505 was at __________.', 'ans': 'Kilwa', 'sol': 'He fortified Kilwa to secure the Swahili Coast passage.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'Almeida was granted the supreme title of __________ to represent the Crown in Asia.', 'ans': 'Viceroy', 'sol': 'वायसराय was the highest administrative title given.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': "The viceroyl's commission was initially limited to a duration of __________ years.", 'ans': 'three', 'sol': 'A three-year term was standard to prevent consolidation of independent power.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The military adversary that Almeida was specifically instructed to neutralize at sea was the __________ Empire.', 'ans': 'Mamluk', 'sol': 'The Mamluk Sultanate of Egypt controlled the spice monopoly.'}, {'type': 'Fill in the Blank', 'q': 'The successor who arrived to replace Almeida in 1508 was Afonso de __________.', 'ans': 'Albuquerque', 'sol': 'Albuquerque arrived with royal orders to take over as governor.'}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': '1505 के अभियान के विवरण का उनकी मात्राओं से मिलान करें:', 'items': [{'left': 'जहाजों की संख्या'}, {'left': 'सैनिकों/पुरुषों की संख्या'}, {'left': 'नियुक्ति का कार्यकाल'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': '21 जहाज'}, {'val': '1', 'text': '1,500 सैनिक'}, {'val': '2', 'text': '3 वर्ष'}], 'sol': 'अल्मेडा 21 जहाजों, 1,500 सैनिकों और 3 साल के कार्यकाल के साथ रवाना हुए।'}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': 'ऐतिहासिक हस्तियों का उनकी प्रशासनिक भूमिकाओं से मिलान करें:', 'items': [{'left': 'राजा मैनुअल प्रथम'}, {'left': 'फ्रांसिस्को डी अल्मेडा'}, {'left': 'अल्फांसो डी अल्बुकर्क'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': 'प्रायोजक राजा'}, {'val': '1', 'text': 'प्रथम नियुक्त वायसराय'}, {'val': '2', 'text': 'नामित दूसरे गवर्नर'}], 'sol': 'राजा मैनुअल प्रथम प्रायोजक थे, अल्मेडा पहले वायसराय थे, और अल्बुकर्क दूसरे गवर्नर थे।'}, {'type': 'Match the Following', 'q': 'अल्मेडा की 1505 की यात्रा के भौगोलिक मील के पत्थरों का उनके क्रम से मिलान करें:', 'items': [{'left': 'प्रस्थान बंदरगाह'}, {'left': 'पूर्वी अफ्रीकी पड़ाव'}, {'left': 'हिंद महासागर द्वीप आधार'}], 'options': [{'val': '0', 'text': 'लिस्बन बंदरगाह'}, {'val': '1', 'text': 'किलवा किला'}, {'val': '2', 'text': 'अंजादीप द्वीप'}], 'sol': 'उन्होंने लिस्बन से प्रस्थान किया, किलवा को मजबूत किया, और अंजादीप में लंगर डाला।'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': "What is the exact date of departure for अल्मेडा's viceregal fleet from लिस्बन?", 'sol': 'उत्तर: March 25, 1505.। स्पष्टीकरण: The fleet left Restelo on March 25, 1505 CE.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': "Who was the Portuguese वायसराय's son who accompanied him on the 1505 voyage?", 'sol': 'उत्तर: Lourenço de अल्मेडा.। स्पष्टीकरण: Lourenço served as a principal captain under his father.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Which battle in Europe gave अल्मेडा the military reputation required for the viceroyalty?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: The Battle of Toro.। स्पष्टीकरण: अल्मेडा showed outstanding valor in the Battle of Toro (1476).'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'What was the name of the state entity established by the Portuguese Crown to govern Asian trade?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: Estado da Índia.। स्पष्टीकरण: The Estado da Índia was the formal state entity.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': "Why did the King restrict the viceroy's term to just three years?", 'sol': 'उत्तर: To prevent the viceroy from establishing independent power.। स्पष्टीकरण: Short tenures ensured absolute loyalty to Lisbon.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Where did अल्मेडा make his first land claim in India?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: Anjadip Island.। स्पष्टीकरण: He landed and began fortification at Anjadip island first.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': 'Which family of Portuguese nobility did अल्मेडा marry into?', 'sol': 'उत्तर: The family of Lanções.। स्पष्टीकरण: He married Maria de Noronha, connected to high nobility.'}, {'type': 'One-Liner', 'q': "What was the primary merchant council in लिस्बन that regulated the वायसराय's trade cargos?", 'sol': 'उत्तर: Casa da Índia.। स्पष्टीकरण: Casa da Índia managed all imperial cargoes and imports.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: King Manuel I appointed Francisco de अल्मेडा as the first वायसराय in 1505.\nकारण: The Portuguese Crown wanted to replace temporary fleets with a permanent administration in India.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'The viceroyalty was created to manage trade permanently.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: अल्मेडा was given a standard three-year term of office.\nकारण: King Manuel I feared that longer tenures would encourage viceroys to declare independence.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Term limits were standard administrative tools for imperial control.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': "अभिकथन: Lourenço de अल्मेडा served as a key naval commander under the वायसराय.\nकारण: He was Francisco de अल्मेडा's only son and a trusted military lieutenant.", 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Lourenço led many crucial patrols on behalf of his father.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: The viceregal instructions ordered the immediate capture of Goa.\nकारण: Goa was the primary administrative base of the Mamluk Sultanate in 1505.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 3, 'sol': 'Both statements are false. Goa was not mentioned in the 1505 instructions, and it was under Bijapur, not Mamluks.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': "अभिकथन: Francisco de अल्मेडा delayed hand over of power to Afonso de Albuquerque in 1508.\nकारण: अल्मेडा disputed the validity of Albuquerque's credentials and sought revenge for his son's death.", 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'अल्मेडा refused to step down until he destroyed the Mamluk fleet at Diu.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: The fleet of 1505 carried a large number of Franciscan friars.\nकारण: The Portuguese expansion combined commercial monopoly goals with Christian missionary zeal.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Religious conversions and missionary presence were integral to Portuguese state policy.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: The Estado da Índia was established as a private joint-stock corporation.\nकारण: The King wanted to minimize financial risks to the royal treasury.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 3, 'sol': 'Both are false. The Estado da Índia was a state-owned crown monopoly, not a private corporation.'}, {'type': 'Assertion-Reason', 'q': 'अभिकथन: अल्मेडा participated in the conquest of Granada before his appointment.\nकारण: Military experience against Muslim states in Spain and North Africa was highly valued by the Portuguese Crown.', 'opts': ['A और R दोनों सही हैं और R, A की सही व्याख्या करता है', 'A और R दोनों सही हैं लेकिन R, A की सही व्याख्या नहीं करता है', 'A सही है लेकिन R गलत है', 'A गलत है लेकिन R सही है'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': "अल्मेडा's experience in the Reconquista made him the ideal candidate to fight Mamluks."}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'Consider the following statements regarding the appointment of फ्रांसिस्को डी अल्मेडा:\n1. He was the first वायसराय of the Estado da Índia.\n2. His appointment was sponsored by King John II in 1498.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['केवल 1', 'केवल 2', '1 और 2 दोनों', 'न तो 1 न ही 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. Statement 2 is incorrect; he was appointed by King Manuel I in 1505.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'Consider the following statements about the 1505 expedition:\n1. The fleet consisted of 21 ships carrying 1,500 soldiers.\n2. The expedition departed from the port of Porto.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['केवल 1', 'केवल 2', '1 और 2 दोनों', 'न तो 1 न ही 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. Statement 2 is incorrect; they departed from Lisbon.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'With reference to the viceregal term of office, consider these statements:\n1. It was set to a non-renewable period of ten years.\n2. Scribes and factors were directly answerable to the वायसराय rather than Lisbon.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['केवल 1', 'केवल 2', '1 और 2 दोनों', 'न तो 1 न ही 2'], 'ans': 3, 'sol': 'Both statements are incorrect. The term was three years, and factors were directly responsible to the Crown (Casa da Índia).'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': "Consider the statements about फ्रांसिस्को डी अल्मेडा's early life:\n1. He gained fame at the Battle of Toro in 1476.\n2. He fought against the Moors in Granada under the Spanish Monarchs.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?", 'opts': ['केवल 1', 'केवल 2', '1 और 2 दोनों', 'न तो 1 न ही 2'], 'ans': 2, 'sol': 'Both statements are correct. अल्मेडा was a veteran of both the Portuguese-Castilian wars and the Granada Reconquista.'}, {'type': 'Statement-Based', 'q': 'With reference to the successor of the first वायसराय, consider these statements:\n1. Afonso de Albuquerque was designated as the second Governor.\n2. Almeida welcomed Albuquerque immediately and transferred all powers in Cochin.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?', 'opts': ['केवल 1', 'केवल 2', '1 और 2 दोनों', 'न तो 1 न ही 2'], 'ans': 0, 'sol': 'Statement 1 is correct. Statement 2 is incorrect; अल्मेडा refused to hand over power and imprisoned Albuquerque.'}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why did King Manuel I establish a permanent viceroyalty in India in 1505?', 'sol': 'To secure the trade routes, manage permanent factories, and counter the Mamluk naval monopoly with a unified military command.'}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why did अल्मेडा refuse to immediately hand over power to Afonso de Albuquerque in 1508?', 'sol': "अल्मेडा wanted to avenge the death of his son Lourenço at Chaul and questioned the validity of Albuquerque's secret patents."}, {'type': 'Why', 'q': 'Why was a three-year term limit imposed on the office of the Portuguese वायसराय?', 'sol': 'To prevent the viceroy from developing a local power base or declaring independence from the Lisbon Crown.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': 'How did the creation of the Estado da Índia change Portuguese operations in the Indian Ocean?', 'sol': 'It transitioned their operations from temporary, seasonal trading expeditions to a permanent political and military administration.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': "How did अल्मेडा's family connections in Portugal influence his appointment as वायसराय?", 'sol': 'As a member of the Counts of Abrantes family, he had direct access to King Manuel I, making him a trusted noble commander.'}, {'type': 'How', 'q': 'How did अल्मेडा assert royal authority over Portuguese merchants operating in India?', 'sol': 'He enforced strict cargo logs, centralized spice purchases at the royal factories, and cracked down on private trade.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': 'Examine the logistical challenges of maintaining a viceroyalty in Cochin from लिस्बन.', 'sol': 'Communication took months, reinforcements were seasonal, and the वायसराय had to act autonomously during crises.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': 'Analyze the conflict between अल्मेडा and Albuquerque regarding the transition of power in 1508-1509.', 'sol': 'The conflict illustrated the clash between two different strategies of empire-building and the problem of verifying royal patents overseas.'}, {'type': 'Case Study', 'q': 'Evaluate the strategic selection of Francisco de अल्मेडा based on his Reconquista military background.', 'sol': 'His experience in Granada made him highly effective at combatting Muslim coalitions but less inclined towards territorial expansion in India.'}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': 'Explain the structure and authority of the Estado da Índia established in 1505.', 'sol': "It was a state-run imperial organization in Asia, headed by a वायसराय who held civil, judicial, and military powers in the King's name."}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': "Describe the role of the 'Capitão-Mor' (Captain-Major) under the वायसरायalty.", 'sol': "The Capitão-Mor commanded individual fleets and patrols, enforcing the वायसराय's naval policies and protecting trade bases."}, {'type': 'Teach the Concept', 'q': 'Explain why the Portuguese Crown prioritized naval governance over land acquisitions in 1505.', 'sol': "Maintaining sea supremacy was cheaper, utilized Portugal's naval technology, and avoided costly conflicts with large Indian mainland states."}]
